# Google issues a "client secret" for Desktop OAuth clients and requires it at
# the token exchange, even though the flow also uses PKCE.
#
# For an installed app it is not a secret in any meaningful sense: it ships
# inside the executable and anyone can read it out. That is exactly why PKCE
# exists, and why Google documents the value as not confidential for this
# client type. It is kept out of the repository anyway, because a public repo
# is a bad place for a credential even when it is a weak one.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value from the Desktop client's
# JSON in Google Cloud Console (APIs & Services -> Credentials).
VITE_GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_SECRET=
